  "id": "COMPOUND:31299 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between 3,5,3'-Trihydroxy-6,7,8,4'-Tetramethoxyflavone and the CD70 antigen, as all three paths point to NCI-H727 as a common target. NCI-H727 is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Talathermophilins A and 1-(1H-indol-6-yl)-3-methylbutan-1-one, all of which are linked to the CD70 antigen. This indicates that the flavone may act as a common target for various compounds that ultimately interact with CD70. The integration of these pathways suggests that the flavone may function as a mediator in the signaling or cellular response pathways involving CD70, potentially through a shared mechanism of action or by modulating the activity of the target compounds. The evidence supports a role for this flavone in the biological context of CD70, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
